The first full gate run exposed a performance bug in the checker—not a mathematical failure. It was repeatedly decoding the same six labels once per product pair, which made the 200,000-sample density test need hundreds of millions of redundant operations. I’m collapsing verification to one decode per supplied label and reusing the exact local color sets; this preserves the witness test while making the mandatory measurement practical.
